<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Valona</h1><p class="st-meta">1346 CE – 1417 CE (approx.) · capital Vlorë</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Albanian coastal lordship around Vlorë and Kanina, founded by a governor of the Serbian Empire and lost to the Ottomans in 1417.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbian-empire">Serbian Empire</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlore">Valona</a> (Vlorë) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanine">Kanina</a> from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> around 1345. His brother-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-komnenos-asen">John Komnenos Asen</a> governed them, and after Dušan's death in 1355 ruled as an independent despot.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its rulers held the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlore">Valona</a>, the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanine">Kanina</a> and nearby lands, trading with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-ragusa">Ragusa</a> and taxing traffic across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-otranto">Strait of Otranto</a>. After John's son Alexander, the city passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balsa-ii">Balša II</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zeta-under-the-balsici">Zeta under the Balšići</a> around 1372, and then through his widow Komita to her son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merksha-zarkovic">Merksha Žarković</a> and, after his death in 1414, to his widow Ruđina.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Ruđina had ruled only briefly when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlore">Valona</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanine">Kanina</a> in 1417. Valona became an Ottoman port and centre of the Sanjak of Avlonya.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-valona.jpg" alt="Principality of Valona" width="320" height="472"><figcaption>Image: Constantine Plakidas · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_southern_Albania,_1410_(cropped).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1346 CE – 1417 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vlorë</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>John Komnenos Asen, Balša II, Merksha Žarković</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian; Greek; Serbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lordship of Valona, Principality of Vlorë</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1382&amp;focus=principality-of-valona" aria-label="Principality of Valona on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5158 732 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Valona lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5478 988L5521 939M5478 988L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5521 939h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5478 988h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5478 988h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vlorë. <a href="/atlas?year=1382&amp;focus=principality-of-valona">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
